{"nodes": [{"id": "method_members_read_ch16x_unit", "label": "READ-ch16x \u2014 main L9494\u2013L9608 (ch. 34 head, \u00a734.1\u2013\u00a734.4), chat 126", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "method/members/READ-ch16x.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "method_members_read_ch16x_16x_01", "label": "16x-01 \u2014 the printed opening sequence overruns the population it is read from (7p at Z = 113)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "method/members/READ-ch16x.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The derivation was validated against the unit's own two anchors (5d at 57, 6d at 89) rather than recited, so the overrun is a measurement and not a reading \u2014 and chat 127's 16z-11 later showed the derivation, not the book, was at fault."}, {"id": "method_members_read_ch16x_16x_02", "label": "16x-02 \u2014 *Seventeen of nineteen* is exact under displacement and false position-by-position", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "method/members/READ-ch16x.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The Madelung order was GENERATED (sort by n+\u2113 then n) rather than recited; the printed 89 % discriminates the conventions, since position-wise would give 79."}, {"id": "method_members_read_ch16x_16x_03", "label": "16x-03 \u2014 \u039b_var carries eleven variables in the main volume and twelve in the Index of Indices", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "method/members/READ-ch16x.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The twelfth is n*, and the Index's own singleton rule depends on it, so as printed the main volume cannot support the compendium's rule."}, {"id": "method_members_read_ch16x_16x_04", "label": "16x-04 \u2014 the radicand is called a count of states and is a count of subshells", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "method/members/READ-ch16x.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "method_members_read_ch16x_16x_05", "label": "16x-05 \u2014 *the provenance of every term is \u00a734.8's table*, and the occupancy q has no row", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "method/members/READ-ch16x.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "method_members_read_ch16x_16x_06", "label": "16x-06 \u2014 Janet dated 1929 in the body and 1928 in the bibliography", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "method/members/READ-ch16x.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "method_members_read_ch16x_16x_07", "label": "16x-07 \u2014 *Both Pauli quantities* names one quantity (2(2\u2113+1)) twice", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "method/members/READ-ch16x.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "method_members_read_ch16x_nu_rule", "label": "The \u03bd rule \u03bd(n,\u2113,q) = n \u2212 a\u00b7\u221a(n \u2212 \u2113 \u2212 1 + q/2(2\u2113+1))", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "method/members/READ-ch16x.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Printed twice and byte-identical on the extracted form; \u00a734.5\u2013\u00a734.7 use it without naming \u03bd, which is why a \u03bd-token probe would have recorded a false defect at L9580's forward pointer."}, {"id": "method_members_read_ch16x_pp_offset_shift", "label": "The Prints & Proofs offset shift \u221294 \u2192 \u221296 is one added post-PP sentence", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "method/members/READ-ch16x.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": 